      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T00:59:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this may regress small folios in 4KB VMAs.\n\n`madvise_folio_pte_batch()` stops at the first slice PTE that is none, maps another folio, or lies past `end`, so `nr \u003c folio_nr_ptes` whenever the window is partly populated, clipped by the VMA or the range, or entered mid-window. The small folio then takes this `continue` on every PTE and is never paged out or deactivated; before this patch it was handled per PTE and checked with `vma_folio_slices_exclusive()`.\n\nCould the skip stay limited to large folios, with the batch only merging young/dirty?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "bea188b10f140ee2fffcc94314caf5a6d016f673",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
